Z||000010||Bob Englert||07-08-2001||07:12 PM||||When I was changing the rack bushing on my Formula, I remember reading in a Pontiac TSB about the changeover from the metal to the plastic rack bushing.  The TSB listed the serial number when the change occured.  I don't have access to the info anymore, but if someone can access the TSB's they should be able to look it up.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000011||Patrick86GT||07-08-2001||09:01 PM||||Thanks to all for your insights.  As w/ all Fiero projects, there are successes....and then there are bumps in the road.<P>I managed to change the steel bushing w/o removing the entire rack, thanks to the snap ring clue and lots of "break away" coupled w/ a propane torch (only a few flare-ups).<BR>Hooray, no more rattle!<P>Once it was down off the jack stands, I went about the AC conversion to R134-A. That went great, too. ICE COLD AC! <P>But, this car that has always run perfectly began to die and run for sh%$ while I was test driving it. With AC on, or with AC OFF...no matter.  <P>Oh well, there's a new chore for next weekend!<P>  ||||reg||1
